# H1 `resize`: the window made smaller, then larger, while the binary runs,
# with a draft in the composer long enough to wrap. Each snap after a resize
# is the binary's own repaint at the new size -- the draft wrapped again, the
# band moved to the new bottom row -- which it draws only once SIGWINCH has
# made it ask the terminal again.
wait 4
type one two three four five six seven eight nine ten eleven twelve thirteen fourteen fifteen sixteen seventeen eighteen nineteen twenty
wait 1
snap start
resize 20x60
wait 1.5
snap small
resize 40x120
wait 1.5
snap large
wire end
